Observation for the reviewer: the token's screen column moves as the Working line's elapsed
clock gains digits ('0s' -> '10s' -> '1m 06s'), so an acceptance click must re-measure the
column ('$D col'/'sed -n 35p') instead of reusing a fixed one. Two earlier attempts missed
the token for exactly that reason; every result recorded above was taken with the column
measured immediately before the click.

Observation 2: the entry exists only while a turn is in flight (plan 'Current state' accepted
this): after '● done' the Working line is replaced by the static 'Worked for … · ☑3/7'
history row, which is deliberately NOT a hit target, so the drawer can no longer be opened
until the next run. Observed at 15:06 on this instance.
